(v) The said FWC shall comprise of the following members:--
2022 SCC OnLine All 395 (a) a young mediator from the Mediation Centre of the district or young advocate having the practices up to five years or senior most student of Vth year, Government Law College or the State University or N.L.Us. having good academic track record and who is public spirited young man, OR;
(b) well acclaimed and recognized social worker of that district having clean antecedant, OR;
(c) retired judicial officers residing in or nearby district, who can devote time for the object of the proceeding OR;
Payasam Sarath Chandra Reddy vs State Of Punjab And Another3 on 2 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/6038239/
3 (d) educated wives of senior judicial or administrative officers of the district.
(vi) The member of the FWC shall never be called as a witness.
(vii) Every complaint or application under Section 498A IPC and other allied sections mentioned above, be immediately referred to Family Welfare Committee by the concerned Magistrate.
